# --- Sign-on ------------------------------------------------------------------
::lines intro
Good evening, wasteland, and welcome to DEADBALL. Chip Vega in the booth, and we've got nine innings of ball for whoever's still got working eyes.
Chip Vega here at the ballpark, where the lights work maybe sixty percent of the time and the hot dogs are legally a dare. Let's play ball.
This is DEADBALL on Coldwater League radio. I'm Chip Vega. Somewhere out there the sun's setting on a stadium that has definitely, definitely been condemned.
Welcome back to the ballgame. Chip Vega, and I'll be your only friend for the next nine innings.
Good evening from the Charles B. Hughson Coliseum. Chip Vega in the booth, and Sir Charles is out front in bronze, same as every night.
::endlines

::lines matchup
Tonight it's the {away} in from out of town to face the {home} on their home dirt.
On the marquee: {away} versus {home}. Two rosters, one working scoreboard, no medical staff.
The {away} take the field against the {home}. Bad blood, worse plumbing. Here we go.
It's {home} hosting {away} under whatever's left of the stadium lights.
::endlines

# --- Matchup WITH standings (used once the league has records on the board) ------
::lines matchup.records
Tonight the {away}, {awayRecord} on the season, roll into town to face the {home} at {homeRecord}.
On the marquee: {away} ({awayRecord}) versus {home} ({homeRecord}). Somebody's record gets worse tonight.
The {away} bring their {awayRecord} mark in against the {home}, sitting at {homeRecord}. Standings on the line, such as they are.
It's {home} ({homeRecord}) hosting {away} ({awayRecord}), two clubs clawing up a league table nobody escapes.
::endlines

# --- Half-inning framing ------------------------------------------------------
::lines half.top
Top of the {inningOrd}. The {team} step up to hit.
Here's the top of the {inningOrd}. {team} coming to bat, the home nine taking the field.
Top {inningOrd}. {team} due up. Let's see who's swinging.
::endlines

::lines half.bottom
Bottom of the {inningOrd}. The home side, the {team}, grab the bats.
Middle of the {inningOrd} behind us, and now the {team} come up for their cuts.
Bottom {inningOrd}, {team} at the plate.
::endlines

# --- Booth chatter: filler BETWEEN outs — weather, the stadium, a raunchy aside,
# --- an obscure stat, or something out of left field. Baseball is long and dry;
# --- Chip fills the dead air. No score/plays here, pure colour. --------------------
::lines chatter
Not much doing out here. Wind's picking up off the flats. Smells like a battery fire, which, to be fair, it usually is.
You can see the haze rolling in over the left-field wall. They painted a distance marker on it once. Nobody's ever reached it. Nobody ever will.
Fun fact: this ballpark was built on a landfill, and on humid nights you can still smell every decision that led us here.
{pitcher} out there on the mound looking like a man who owes money to everyone in this stadium. Which, in fairness, he might.
The grounds crew tried to reseed the infield last spring. It came up brown and angry and now they just rake it and apologize.
I'm told the record for longest game at this park is fourteen hours. Seven people finished it. Two of them on purpose.
Somebody in the bleachers just took their shirt off. It's nine degrees out. I'm not going to editorialize, but I have concerns.
Weather's holding, which around here means the acid's only a light drizzle. Bring an umbrella, lose an umbrella. That's the deal.
They sell a hot dog here called the Widowmaker. It comes with a waiver. I've had three.
Little-known stat: no left-handed batter has hit safely at this park after sundown since the lights started flickering. Draw your own conclusions.
The {team} bullpen's been quiet. Then again, half of them are asleep and one of them, I believe, is technically deceased.
Quiet moment out here. Good time to mention the bathrooms are out of order. All of them. Have been since the last administration.
You know, my ex-wife loved this game. Sat right there in section nine. Section nine is a crater now. Life comes at you fast.
Ballpark organist is playing something in a minor key again. He only knows the one song. It's about drowning.
Vendor just walked past selling something he called "meat adjacent." I didn't follow up. I value what's left of me.
The stadium clock froze at 6:66 four years ago and honestly it's never been wrong about the mood.
Somewhere out past the outfield wall a dog is howling in perfect rhythm with the crowd. Nobody brought a dog.
They retired a number here once. Not for a player. For a guy who survived a full season in the cheap seats. Brave soul.
Folks ask me who Sir Charles was. He owned this ground. Halcyon offered him a fortune for it three times, and three times he sent the cheque back with two tickets in the envelope.
People rub the shoes on the Sir Charles statue out front for luck. The shoes are gold now. The luck's still bronze.
They keep Sir Charles's seat behind home plate empty. Nobody sits in it. Not even the drunks, and that's saying something.
Halcyon built a whole estate round this ballpark because Sir Charles wouldn't sell. You can still see the offices sulking over the left-field wall.
The Basin Blue Birds are the oldest club in this league. They were playing ball in Old Coldwater when the Meridian still had a doorman.
The Coldwater Crows go back to 2022, before the Curtain went up. One club in this league is older, and the Crows have spent every season since trying to bury it.
Blue Birds and Crows. Oldest grudge in the Basin. Nobody remembers what started it, and everybody remembers whose side they're on.
Sir Charles was a Blue Birds man. Never missed a home game, never said a kind word about the Crows, and the Crows have never said one back.
Never been a wire in a Crows uniform. Not one augment, not one graft, not since 2022. Ask them why and they just smile at you. Politely. For a long time.
The Crows don't sign free agents. Somebody vouches for you, you sit a season in the stands, and one day there's a jersey in your locker. Nobody ever says who left it.
You'll see crows on the light towers on game nights. Just sitting. Watching. The Crows' people say that's lucky. They don't say for who.
::endlines

# --- Balls in play ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The server decides where every ball in play goes and who fields it, and the line has to
# agree with the picture. A pool named for a kind of play (atbat.flyout) airs on every play
# of that kind, so its lines say nothing that's true of only some of them: no direction,
# depth or kind of catch. A pool with a tag after it (atbat.flyout.diving) airs only on a
# play that carries the tag, in the draw beside the bare pool's lines. The tags are listed
# in docs/bsm-format.md, and regress fails a bare line that names a direction.
# {fielder} is the man who fielded it, as "the shortstop". {diver} is the man who dove for
# a hit and missed. {feet} is how far a home run went.

# --- Routine outs -------------------------------------------------------------
::lines atbat.strikeout
{batter} goes down swinging. {pitcher} blows it right past him. That's {outs} away.
Strike three, {batter}'s frozen. {pitcher} owns him. {outs} down.
{batter} waves at a nasty one from {pitcher} and sits. {outs} gone in the frame.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout
{batter} grounds out to {fielder}. {outs} away.
Ground ball, {batter}, and {fielder} makes the play. {outs} down.
{batter} puts it on the ground. {fielder} takes care of him. {outs} in the books.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.routine
{batter} hits it right at {fielder}. Routine, and he's out. {outs} away.
Ground ball off the bat of {batter}, easy play, one more gone. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.ranging
{fielder} has to range for that one, and he gets there. {batter} is out. {outs} away.
{batter} makes {fielder} run for it, and he still makes the play. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.diving
{fielder} dives, knocks it down, gets up and gets him! {outs} away.
Diving stop by {fielder}! He gets {batter} by a step. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.barehand
Slow roller. {fielder} charges, picks it up bare-handed and throws him out. {outs} away.
{batter} barely gets wood on it, and {fielder} comes in, bare hand, throws on the run. Out. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.comebacker
Comebacker to {pitcher}. He gloves it and lobs it to first. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.catcher
{batter} taps it in front of the plate. The catcher pounces and throws him out. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.dirt
The throw from {fielder} is in the dirt, and the first baseman digs it out. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.pull
{batter} rolls over on it. Grounder, out at first. {outs} in the books.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.left
{batter} grounds one to the left side, and {fielder} throws him out. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.groundout.right
Ground ball to the right side. {fielder} handles it, and that's {outs}.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout
Fly ball, {batter}. {fielder} puts it away. {outs} down.
{batter} lifts it to the outfield, and {fielder} makes the catch. {outs} away.
{batter} flies out to {fielder}. {outs} gone.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.routine
{batter} lifts it to the outfield. {fielder} is camped under it. {outs} away.
{batter} gets air but not enough. Run-of-the-mill flyout. {outs} gone.
Fly ball, and {fielder} barely has to move. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.ranging
{fielder} gets on his horse and runs it down. {outs} away.
{batter} makes {fielder} run a long way for it, and he gets there. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.diving
{fielder} lays out... and he CATCHES it! {batter} robbed of a hit. {outs} away.
That's dropping in... no! {fielder} dives and comes up with it. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.sliding
{fielder} comes in hard, slides, and takes it off his shoe tops. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.leaping
{batter} drives it to the wall... {fielder} leaps... and pulls it down! {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.robbed
That ball is gone... NO! {fielder} reaches over the wall and takes a home run away from {batter}! {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.track
Way back, {fielder} on the track, and he gets it. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.deep
{batter} hits it a long way, but it stays in the yard. {fielder} catches it. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.shallow
Shallow fly. {fielder} comes in and takes it. {outs} gone.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.gap
{batter} hits it into the gap, but {fielder} gets over there. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.flyout.line
Fly ball toward the line. {fielder} drifts over and makes the catch. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout
{batter} pops it up. {fielder} squeezes it. {outs} away.
Pop-up off {batter}'s bat. {fielder} calls for it and takes it. {outs} down.
{batter} gets under it. Pop-up to {fielder}, caught. {outs} in the frame.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.infield
{batter} pops it straight up. {fielder} circles under it and gloves it. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.fair
Little pop-up off {batter}'s bat, caught in fair territory. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.foul
{batter} lifts a pop foul, and {fielder} drifts over and takes it. {outs} away.
Pop foul. {fielder} tracks it into foul ground and squeezes it. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.rail
Pop foul toward the seats. {fielder} leans over the rail and catches it among the fans. {outs} down.
{fielder} reaches into the first row for it, and he has it. Somebody's beer is gone. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.shallow
{batter} skies one into the shallow outfield, and {fielder} goes back for it. {outs} in the frame.
::endlines

::lines atbat.popout.catcher
The catcher throws off the mask, finds it, and squeezes it. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.out
{batter} is retired. {outs} away.
That's {batter} put out. {outs} down.
::endlines

# --- Non-scoring baserunners --------------------------------------------------
::lines atbat.single
Base hit, {batter}. He's aboard.
{batter} singles. The {team} have a runner.
{batter} finds a way on. Single.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.gap
{batter} slaps a clean single into the gap and takes first.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.late
Base hit, {batter}! He beats it out and stands on first.
{batter} legs it out. The throw's too late, and it's an infield hit.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.hole
{batter} punches one through the infield. Runner aboard.
{batter} finds the hole. Base hit.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.middle
Right back up the middle! {batter} singles past {pitcher}.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.liner
{batter} lines one into the outfield for a base hit.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.bloop
{batter} bloops one in. Nobody's getting to that. Single.
A little flare off the end of the bat drops in. Base hit, {batter}.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.dove
{batter} rips one past a diving {diver}. Base hit.
{diver} lays out for it and comes up empty. {batter} has a single.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.wide
{fielder} makes the stop, but the throw pulls the first baseman off the bag. {batter} is safe.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.barehand
{fielder} barehands it and fires... too late. {batter} beats it out.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.diving
Diving stop by {fielder}, but there's no play. Infield hit, {batter}.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.catcher
{batter} dribbles one in front of the plate, and the catcher has no play.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.comebacker
{pitcher} knocks it down but can't make the play. Infield hit, {batter}.
::endlines

::lines atbat.single.line
{batter} hits one down the line, and it's a single.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double
Double for {batter}. He's in scoring position.
{batter} gets two on it. Runner on second.
That's extra bases for {batter}. A double.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.line
{batter} rips it down the line, into the corner, he's got two!
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.wall
{batter} drives one to the wall and pulls into second. Two-bagger.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.offwall
Off the wall! {fielder} plays the carom, but {batter} is in at second.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.gap
Into the gap goes {batter}'s drive, and he's into second with a double.
{batter} splits the outfielders. Double.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.standup
{batter} goes into second standing up. Standing double.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.slide
{batter} slides into second ahead of the throw. Double.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.dove
{diver} dives and misses, and {batter} is into second.
::endlines

::lines atbat.double.liner
A screamer off {batter}'s bat, and he's into second with a double.
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple
{batter} hits one to the deep part of the yard and keeps going. Triple!
Triple for {batter}! He's ninety feet from home.
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple.slide
{batter} drives it deep and wheels around, he's flying, and he slides into THIRD! Triple!
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple.offwall
Way back, off the wall, {batter} is churning, and he's in with a triple!
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple.standup
{batter} goes into third standing up. A stand-up triple!
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple.gap
{batter} splits the outfielders and doesn't stop till third. What a leg on him.
::endlines

::lines atbat.triple.line
Down the line and into the corner! {batter} is around second and into third. Triple.
::endlines

::lines atbat.walk
{pitcher} loses the zone. {batter} takes ball four and trots to first.
Four wide ones, {batter} draws the walk. Free pass.
{batter} spits on a full count and takes his base. {pitcher} not happy about it.
::endlines

# --- Sim v2: hit batters and errors (plate appearances) ------------------------
# {fielder} is the fielder charged, as "the shortstop". The throwing error is its own
# pool because the batter takes second on it; the bare pool keeps him at first. A
# fielding error is a grounder booted or through his legs, or a fly ball dropped, so the
# bare pool says none of those.
::lines atbat.hitbypitch
{pitcher} comes inside and plunks {batter}. He takes his base, slowly, and says something on the way.
That one gets {batter} on the elbow. Hit by pitch. He shakes it off and jogs to first.
{batter} wears one from {pitcher}. Free base, and a bruise to go with it.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error
Error on {fielder}, and {batter} is on first.
{fielder} can't handle it. {batter} is aboard on the error.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.boot
{batter} hits it right at {fielder}, and he boots it. Error, and {batter}'s aboard.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.ground
Grounder to {fielder}, and he can't come up with it. {batter} reaches on the error.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.legs
It goes right through {fielder}'s legs. {batter} is safe at first, and the crowd lets {fielder} hear about it.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.drop
Fly ball to {fielder}... and he drops it! {batter} is on with an error.
{fielder} gets under it and it pops out of his glove. Error, and {batter} is aboard.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.throwing
{fielder} gets to it, then throws it away. {batter} takes second on the error.
Bad throw by {fielder}. {batter} is all the way to second.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.throwing.stands
{fielder} fields it clean and throws it into the stands. {batter} is waved on to second.
::endlines

::lines atbat.error.throwing.past
The throw from {fielder} sails past first and rolls toward the corner. {batter} takes second on the error.
::endlines

# --- Situational outs: double plays, sac flies, productive groundouts -----------
::lines atbat.doubleplay
Two for the price of one. {batter} bounces into a double play. The {team} dugout deflates. {outs} gone.
Double play. {batter} erases the runner and himself. {outs} down.
They turn two on {batter}. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.routine
{batter} raps into a tailor-made double play. {pitcher} exhales; the whole frame's undone in one pitch. {outs} down.
{batter} hits it right at 'em and they flip it around for a double play. Cruel game. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.ranging
{fielder} ranges over for it, and they turn two anyway. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.diving
{fielder} dives, scrambles up, and they still turn two! {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.543
Ground ball, and they turn TWO on {batter}! Around the horn, rally strangled in the crib. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.643
Short to second to first, and that's two. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.463
Second to short to first. They turn two on {batter}. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.363
First to short and back to first. A double play you don't see every night. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.doubleplay.163
Back to {pitcher}, who turns and throws to second, and on to first. Double play. {outs} down.
::endlines

# --- Triple play: roughly one game in five hundred. Chip has never seen one either.
# It's always 5-4-3: the third baseman steps on third and throws round the horn.
::lines atbat.tripleplay
THREE. That's three outs on one pitch. {batter} hit into a triple play and the {team} bench doesn't know where to look. Nobody move. I need a minute.
{batter} rolls one into the teeth of it and they turn a TRIPLE play. Folks, whatever you paid to get in here, you're square with the house. Inning over.
::endlines

::lines atbat.tripleplay.543
Ground ball to the left side and... they got one, they got two, THEY GOT THREE. Triple play. {batter} into a triple play. I have called this game eleven years and I have never said that sentence.
Around the horn: third, second, first, all of it, all at once. Triple play on {batter}. The inning is over and it never really started. {pitcher} just walks off like it is nothing. It isn't nothing.
::endlines

::lines atbat.sacfly
Deep enough! {batter} lifts a sacrifice fly, the runner tags from third and scores. He's out, but it counts on the board. {outs} away.
Sac fly off the bat of {batter}. {team} do it the ugly way. Run's in, {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.sacfly.track
{batter} gives himself up, fly ball to the track, the runner trots home. Traded an out for a run. {outs} down.
::endlines

::lines atbat.sacfly.home
{fielder} makes the catch and throws home, but the runner beats it. Sac fly, {batter}. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines atbat.productout
Groundout by {batter}, does his job, moves the runner over. {outs} down.
{batter} grounds one that scoots the runner up. Nothing pretty, but it plays. {outs} in the frame.
::endlines

::lines atbat.productout.right
{batter} rolls out to the right side but pushes the runner up ninety feet. A productive out, if there's such a thing in this town. {outs} away.
::endlines

# --- Sim v2: the running game ---------------------------------------------------
# {runner} is the man running. {base} is the bag in play: the one he's going for on a
# steal, the one he's standing on for a pickoff or a throw over.
::lines run.steal
{runner} takes off, and he's in there! Stolen base. {runner} on {base}.
Here goes {runner}. The throw's late. He swipes {base}.
{pitcher} is slow to the plate and {runner} makes him pay. That's a steal of {base}.
::endlines

::lines run.caughtstealing
{runner} is going, and the throw is there! Caught stealing. {outs} away.
The catcher pops up and fires, tag applied. {runner} is out at {base}. {outs} down.
{runner} tries for {base} and gets thrown out by a step. {outs} gone.
::endlines

::lines run.pickoff
{pitcher} spins and throws to {base}, and {runner} is picked off! {outs} away.
{runner} wanders too far off {base} and {pitcher} catches him leaning. Picked off. {outs} down.
{runner} gets hung up off {base}, and they run him down. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines run.throwover
{pitcher} throws over to {base}. {runner} dives back in time.
Throw over. {runner} gets back. The crowd lets {pitcher} know what it thinks of that.
{pitcher} checks {runner}, steps off, throws over. Safe. We go again.
::endlines

::lines run.doublesteal
Double steal! Both runners go, and nobody throws. The {team} have two in scoring position.
They're both running, and they both make it. A double steal.
::endlines

::lines run.doublesteal.out
Both runners go, and they nail {runner} at {base}. The trail man moves up on the throw. {outs} away.
::endlines

::lines run.wildpitch
That one gets past the catcher! Wild pitch, and the runners move up.
{pitcher} bounces one in the dirt and it skips to the backstop. Wild pitch. Runners advance.
::endlines

::lines run.wildpitch.score
Wild pitch! It gets away, and {runner} comes in to score!
{pitcher} buries one in the dirt, it rolls to the backstop, and {runner} trots home. A run on a wild pitch.
::endlines

::lines run.passedball
The catcher can't hold on to it. Passed ball, and the runners move up.
That one goes right through the catcher's mitt. Passed ball. Everybody moves up a base.
::endlines

::lines run.passedball.score
Passed ball! It rolls to the screen and {runner} scores from third.
::endlines

# --- Runs batted in (non-home-run scoring play) -------------------------------
# A single, a double or a triple that scored runs: the bare lines say none of which.
::lines rbi
Base knock for {batter}, and the {team} cash in.
{batter} comes through with runners on. {rbi} in! Big swing for the {team}.
Clutch hit, {batter}! That's {rbi} in for the {team}. The dugout's on its feet.
::endlines

::lines rbi.gap
{batter} drives one into the gap, and that brings in {rbi}!
::endlines

::lines rbi.line
{batter} drives {rbi} home with a shot down the line. The {team} strike.
::endlines

::lines rbi.wall
{batter} goes to the wall with it, and the {team} score.
::endlines

::lines rbi.dove
Past a diving {diver}, and the {team} score!
::endlines

::lines rbi.bloop
{batter} bloops one in, and the {team} score. Ugly and effective.
::endlines

::lines rbi.late
{batter} beats out the throw, and the {team} score on the play.
::endlines

# --- Home runs ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every home run goes over the wall; the tags say how: nodoubt, scraper (just over),
# pole (off the foul pole) and leap (an outfielder jumps for it at the wall).
::lines hr.solo
SWING and a long drive by {batter}... see ya! Solo homer, over the wall for the {team}!
{batter} launches it into the dark. Solo bomb. One run in for the {team}.
::endlines

::lines hr.solo.nodoubt
{batter} crushes one and it's GONE! A solo shot, no doubt about it, and {team} tack on a run!
{batter} hits it {feet} feet. Solo shot. The outfielders don't bother moving.
::endlines

::lines hr.solo.scraper
{batter} hits it high and deep... it's got enough! Just over the wall. Solo home run.
::endlines

::lines hr.solo.pole
Off the foul pole! That's a solo home run for {batter}.
::endlines

::lines hr.solo.leap
{fielder} goes up at the wall... and it's over his glove! Solo home run, {batter}.
::endlines

::lines hr.grand
{batter} unloads with the bases juiced. GRAND SLAM! Four runs! The {team} blow it open!
Get up, get outta here! {batter} just hit a GRAND SLAM! Bases cleared, {rbi} runs, {team} take over!
Bases loaded, and {batter} demolishes it! Grand slam! Four come around for the {team}!
::endlines

::lines hr
{batter} crushes it. Outta here! A {rbi}-run homer for the {team}!
Gone! {batter} goes deep, {rbi} runs score for the {team}!
{batter} parks one over the fence, {rbi} in on the blast. {team} answer.
::endlines

::lines hr.nodoubt
Long gone! {batter} hits it {feet} feet, and {rbi} runs score for the {team}!
::endlines

::lines hr.scraper
{batter} hits it to the wall... and over! Barely. A {rbi}-run homer for the {team}.
::endlines

::lines hr.pole
Off the foul pole! A {rbi}-run home run for {batter}!
::endlines

::lines hr.leap
{fielder} jumps at the wall and comes down empty. {rbi}-run homer, {batter}!
::endlines

# --- Running score, called after every scoring play ---------------------------
::lines score.update
That makes it {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}.
Score check: {home} {homeScore}, {away} {awayScore}.
On the board: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}. {leader} out in front by {lead}.
New numbers: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}.
::endlines

# When the run ties it: score.update's leader line has nobody to name.
::lines score.tied
That ties it. {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}.
All square: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}.
Dead level at {awayScore} apiece. We've got a ballgame.
::endlines

# --- Occasional score checkpoint (end of every third inning) ------------------
::lines recap.half
After {inningOrd}: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}. Grab a beer, it won't help.
Three in the books at the turn of the {inningOrd}: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}.
Where we stand through {inningOrd}: {home} {homeScore}, {away} {awayScore}.
::endlines

# --- Walk-off (home team takes a late lead and the game ends) ------------------
::lines walkoff
AND THAT'LL DO IT! {batter} wins it for the {home}! The crowd, the four of them, go absolutely feral!
WALK-OFF! {batter} sends everyone home! {home} take it, {homeScore} to {awayScore}!
Ballgame over! {batter} is a hero in a town that eats its heroes! {home} win it in walk-off fashion!
::endlines

# --- Extra innings: tied after nine. We cut in only for the plays that matter. The
# --- deeper it goes the harder both sides swing, so somebody breaks it — soon. ------
::lines extras.intro
Nine wasn't enough. We're going to EXTRA INNINGS, folks. Nobody in this crumbling barn gets to go home yet.
Tied after nine. Free baseball, and around here 'free' means it costs you your whole night and possibly a lung.
We spill into extras, dead even. Somewhere a generator groans. Bats are getting angry. This ends soon, one way or another.
::endlines

::lines extras.top
We cut back in. Top of the {inningOrd}, {team} up, still level. Everybody's swinging for keeps now.
Top of the {inningOrd}, extras, and the {team} are hacking at everything. Something's gotta give.
::endlines

::lines extras.bottom
Bottom of the {inningOrd}, still knotted, and the {team} get their cuts to end it right here.
Home half of the {inningOrd}. The {team} looking for the one run that sends everybody home.
::endlines

# --- Home half in extras while TRAILING: they must answer or it's over ------------
::lines extras.bottom.trail
The {leader} grabbed the lead up top. Bottom of the {inningOrd}, and the {team} are down to their last cuts to answer it.
Home half of the {inningOrd}, {team} trailing by {lead}. Answer now or the season ends here. For tonight, anyway.
Bottom {inningOrd}, backs to the wall. The {team} need {lead} just to breathe, or it's over.
::endlines

::lines extras.cut
Extra innings roll on, and both dugouts smell blood.
::endlines

::lines extras.hold
...and they go quietly. Still level. On we go, the bats getting meaner by the inning.
Nothing across. Still tied. Nobody said this town does mercy.
Three up, three down, and we're still deadlocked: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}. Somebody end this.
::endlines

# --- Top-half go-ahead in extras that the home side can't answer = a road win ------
::lines winning.top
The {leader} pushed across the go-ahead in the {inningOrd} and the home side had NOTHING in reply. That's your ballgame.
That run in the top of the {inningOrd} stands up, and the {leader} steal it on the road and get out of town alive.
Go-ahead run in extras, home half comes up empty, and the {leader} make it stick. Ballgame.
::endlines

# --- THE CRACK: what the booth says as the ball comes off the bat -----------------------
# Said before anyone knows how it ends, so nothing here may give it away: no "base hit", no "he's
# got it". {toward} is where it's going ("toward third", "to right-centre"); the .hard and .soft
# pools are a ball hit past 100 mph or under 70. Tag suffixes (.left, .deep...) are the
# CONTACT_TAGS in plugins/broadcast/sports/baseball.js.
::lines contact.ground
On the ground {toward}.
Bounding ball {toward}.
Hit on the ground, {toward}.
Grounder {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.ground.hard
Smoked on the ground {toward}!
Rocket of a grounder {toward}!
Hammered into the dirt {toward}!
Sharp one {toward}!
::endlines

::lines contact.ground.soft
Topped, rolling slow {toward}.
Little nubber {toward}.
Chopped, and it's dying {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.ground.comebacker
Right back up the box!
Back at the pitcher's feet!
::endlines

::lines contact.ground.line
Down the line!
::endlines

::lines contact.liner
Lined {toward}!
Line drive {toward}!
On a line {toward}!
::endlines

::lines contact.liner.hard
Scorched on a line {toward}!
Frozen rope {toward}!
That's a laser {toward}!
::endlines

::lines contact.liner.soft
Soft liner {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.fly
Fly ball {toward}.
Lifted {toward}.
Up in the air {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.fly.hard
Drive! Way back {toward}!
Crushed! Deep {toward}!
He got all of that one, {toward}!
::endlines

::lines contact.fly.soft
Lazy fly {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.fly.deep
Hit well, going back {toward}!
That's got some carry {toward}!
::endlines

::lines contact.fly.shallow
Looper {toward}.
Shallow fly {toward}.
::endlines

::lines contact.pop
Popped up {toward}.
Sky-high pop-up {toward}.
Straight up, and it's still going up.
::endlines

::lines contact.pop.foul
Popped up, drifting into foul ground.
::endlines

::lines contact.pop.catcher
Popped straight up behind the plate.
::endlines

# --- THE CURTAIN CALL: one game, top two teams, winner takes the season (the pools keep the old key) ---------------
::lines worldseries.intro
This is it. THE CURTAIN CALL. One game, two clubs, and a whole miserable season of baseball comes down to the next nine innings. Chip Vega, and I have never been more awake.
Welcome to the DEADBALL CURTAIN CALL. Winner takes the crown, loser takes the long walk home. Chip Vega in the booth, gripping the desk so hard my knuckles went.
Nine innings from immortality. The Curtain Call, folks. Last game of the season, and somebody's about to become a legend in a town that forgets fast.
They call it the Curtain Call because it's the last act of the season, and because the Curtain is the one thing in this city nobody's knocked down. Yet. Chip Vega, let's go.
::endlines

::lines worldseries.matchup
For all of it: the {away} versus the {home}. Two survivors, one trophy, no tomorrow.
The {away} ({awayRecord}) against the {home} ({homeRecord}), the two best clubs left standing, playing for the only thing that ever mattered.
Winner takes the season, loser takes nothing. {away} and {home}. Let's settle it.
::endlines

::lines worldseries.final
IT'S OVER! The {leader} are your DEADBALL CURTAIN CALL CHAMPIONS! {home} {homeScore}, {away} {awayScore}. Carve it into whatever's still standing!
CHAMPIONS! The {leader} take the whole thing, {homeScore} to {awayScore}! A season of blood and rust, and they're the last ones grinning!
That's your ballgame and your SEASON! The {leader} take the Curtain Call! {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}. Somewhere, a bookie weeps into his ledger.
::endlines

::lines worldseries.outro
The {leader} are champions. The rest of us go back to nothing. Chip Vega. Good night, and long live the kings, however briefly.
Champions crowned, season buried. Chip Vega signing off on the Curtain Call. Same dirt tomorrow, but tonight belongs to the {leader}.
::endlines

# --- Final ---------------------------------------------------------------------
::lines final
That's the ballgame. Final score: {home} {homeScore}, {away} {awayScore}. {leader} take it by {lead}.
And it's over after {inningOrd}. {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}, {leader} on top.
Ballgame. {leader} win it, {homeScore} to {awayScore}. Somewhere, a bookie is smiling.
Final from the ballpark: {away} {awayScore}, {home} {homeScore}. {leader} get it done.
::endlines

# --- Sign-off ------------------------------------------------------------------
::lines outro
That's DEADBALL. {leader} take the day. Chip Vega saying: go home, lock the door, and dream of extra innings.
For the {leader} and everyone still upright out there, this has been Chip Vega. Good night, and mind the radiation.
Chip Vega, signing off. Same dirt, same dread, tomorrow. Stay off the field.
::endlines

END
